## DESCRIPTION
## Asks the student to calculated the determinant of a 2 by 2 matrix.
## ENDDESCRIPTION


## DBsubject(Linear algebra)
## DBchapter(Determinants)
## DBsection(Computing determinants)
## Date(September 5, 2008)
## Institution(Fitchburg State University)
## Author(Peter Staab)
## KEYWORDS('determinant','2 by 2 matrix')

# updated 2022.10.29

DOCUMENT();    # This should be the first executable line in the problem.
loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');

do {
    $A = Matrix([ [ random(-6, 6), random(-6, 6) ],
        [ random(-6, 6), random(-6, 6) ] ]);
    $det = Real($A->det);
} while ($det == 0);

BEGIN_PGML
If
[```A = [$A] ```]

Then [` |A| = `] [___]{$det}

END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
Using the rule for determinants of 2 by 2 matrices which is if
[``` A = \begin{bmatrix} a & b \\ c & d \end{bmatrix} ```]
then
[``` |A| = ad-bc ```]

In this case, [`|A|=[$det]`]
END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();
